WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.440
Application security matters for SaaS and cloud environments because customers trust

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:09.780
hosted systems with sensitive data, workflows, integrations, and identity information.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.440
A weakness in an application can become a direct risk to confidentiality, availability,

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.220
processing integrity, or customer trust.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:21.800
OWASP provides community-driven application security guidance.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.500
The OWASP Top 10 gives development, DevSecOps, security,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.120
and compliance teams a common language for discussing the most important web application

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:36.140
risks. SOC 2 reports evaluate controls against Trust Services Criteria.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:41.800
The Security category is required for SOC 2 and focuses on protecting systems and data

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.700
through logical access,

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.880
system operations, change management, risk mitigation, and monitoring.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:54.140
Application security supports SOC 2 by making controls practical inside the software

00:00:54.360 --> 00:01:00.120
delivery lifecycle. Secure coding, access control, monitoring, vulnerability management,

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:04.100
and change management all produce the operational evidence auditors expect.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.760
Each module explains an OWASP risk, practical attack examples, mitigations,

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:13.260
and selected SOC 2 Trust Services Criteria mappings.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:15.800
The mappings support awareness and planning,

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.540
but they do not replace formal audit scoping or control testing.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:23.200
Use OWASP categories to organize application risk work.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:27.820
Use SOC 2 criteria to connect technical safeguards to control objectives.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:33.400
Validate mappings with the organization's security, compliance, and audit stakeholders.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:39.460
Selected SOC 2 mappings for this topic include CC3.2 - Risk identification;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:46.000
CC7.1 - Vulnerability management; CC8.1 - Change management processes.
